From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CrashSystemZ <100166199+CrashSystemZ@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:36:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Start child processes with the loader named by
 WINELOADER.

A process Wine starts runs the loader beside ntdll.so, whatever loader the first process
ran. A launcher that starts a game from a copy of the loader inside an app bundle (so that
macOS takes the process for that app, and gives it Game Mode) lost that with the first
child: a game started by a stub (Unreal's Game.exe starting Game-Win64-Shipping.exe) ran
as plain Wine.

With WINELOADER set to an absolute path of an executable, child processes run that loader.
The variable is inherited, so the whole process tree does. The loader must have ntdll.so
beside it, as any copy of the loader has to.

Original work for Hamster Launcher (LGPL-2.1-or-later).

Topic: host-loader
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
@@ -393,6 +393,7 @@ static void set_config_dir(void)
 static void init_paths(void)
 {
     Dl_info info;
+    const char *loader;
 
     if (!dladdr( init_paths, &info ) || !(ntdll_dir = realpath_dirname( info.dli_fname )))
         fatal_error( "cannot get path to ntdll.so\n" );
@@ -408,6 +409,11 @@ static void init_paths(void)
         bin_dir = build_relative_path( dll_dir, LIBDIR "/wine", BINDIR );
         data_dir = build_relative_path( dll_dir, LIBDIR "/wine", DATADIR "/wine" );
         wineloader = build_path( ntdll_dir, "wine" );
+        /* A launcher that starts Wine from a copy of this loader inside an app bundle names the
+         * copy here, so that child processes run it too. macOS knows a process by the app whose
+         * main executable it is: one that runs this loader is nobody's, and gets no Game Mode. */
+        if ((loader = getenv( "WINELOADER" )) && loader[0] == '/' && !access( loader, X_OK ))
+            wineloader = strdup( loader );
     }
 
     set_dll_path();
